From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32: SIO_UDP_CONNRESET, DisconnectEx socket reuse, WSACancelAsyncRequest, WSAJoinLeaf and more (3715)

ws2_32: SIO_UDP_CONNRESET (ICMP port unreachable on UDP), DisconnectEx(TF_REUSE_SOCKET), WSACancelAsyncRequest, WSApSetPostRoutine, WPUCompleteOverlappedRequest, WSAJoinLeaf, WSAGetQOSByName

CORE review (wineserver sock.c, ntdll unix socket/server/file). No new server
request: two new AFD ioctls (306, 307), so only server, ntdll.so and ws2_32 change.
See patches/notes/3715.txt for behaviour, limits and what is guessed.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 3279 (fast-a): WSAGetQOSByName was implemented by 3279 and 3715 (and drafter 7's 5511); 3715's kept (RECONCILE-CLOUD ws2_32 verdict KEEP-A=3715; it follows the documented template enumeration: an empty name string in a buffer of non-zero length lists the (no) templates). 3279's version and mutant SG_MUTANT_WSAQOS dropped.
